{:db/id 17592186147456 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186147393 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eef27d2b-6149-5070-b711-f4dcc7db2a03" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b5189ec2-ea1c-5036-9543-b963bd072ab7" :question/math-academy-id "e-9069" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\n- $y\\,y' + x^2y^2 = e^x y^4$\n\n- $xy' + x^3y = -x^2 y^3$\n\n- $y' + y\\cos{x} = e^{y+1}$" :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{{\\rm{d}}y}}{{{\\rm{d}}x}} + p(x)y= q(x)y^n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Bernoulli differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\ny' + x^2y = e^x y^3\n$$\n\nwhich is a Bernoulli differential equation with\n\n$$\np(x) = x^2, \\qquad q(x) = e^x, \\qquad n=3.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is a Bernoulli differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\ny' + x^2y = -xy^3\n$$\n\nwhich is a Bernoulli differential equation with\n\n$$\np(x) = x^2, \\qquad q(x) =-x, \\qquad n=3.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $q(x)y^n$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eef27d2b-6149-5070-b711-f4dcc7db2a03" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049592}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186147729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eef27d2b-6149-5070-b711-f4dcc7db2a03" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7400fe2-57e2-5a4e-bded-f9b2de6b23cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186144138} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2852ec-dbe6-5b4c-ad88-11e744ebde41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186144139} {:answer/id #uuid "f0ca9576-4d88-545f-befd-42ba5b33586a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186144140} {:answer/id #uuid "f88c153a-a6e9-58ba-bd4f-06467d0c8b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id 17592186144141} {:answer/id #uuid "3cdeff55-d770-5e4a-add0-f7f885d99ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186144142}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3f84493d-f98d-517e-a5a1-fe871019e01f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186144137}] :question/id #uuid "7b913b73-c105-5ba7-b06a-20d353f239e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-108446" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\n1. $y^{′} + x^{2}y = xy^{2}$\n2. $y^{′} + x^{2}y^{2} = xy^{3}$\n3. $y^{′} + x^{2}y = \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{y}}$"} {:db/id 17592186147730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eef27d2b-6149-5070-b711-f4dcc7db2a03" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab2f4026-36e6-5fbc-833b-decd18f6a835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186144144} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4faf50-366b-579d-a717-61a2ca691125" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186144145} {:answer/id #uuid "015491ea-883d-52af-973e-04ddfc150ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given equations is a Bernoulli differential equation" :db/id 17592186144146} {:answer/id #uuid "72a8162a-08dd-5d0b-805f-010927f5c146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186144147} {:answer/id #uuid "771e905b-a148-5e10-8532-569befd71d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id 17592186144148}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c43c6790-ab66-5b2b-9d5c-3664185f108c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186144143}] :question/id #uuid "5064d2f0-3231-54a8-845d-9b0beda86f87" :question/math-academy-id "q-108447" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\n1. $yy^{′} + x^{2}y^{3} = e^{x}y^{4}$\n2. $y^{2}y^{′} + x^{2}y^{3} = e^{x}y^{4}$\n3. $y^{′} + x^{2}\\sin y = x\\cos^{3} y$"} {:db/id 17592186244191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eef27d2b-6149-5070-b711-f4dcc7db2a03" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb9d536d-0e0e-56d0-b075-65f0dfbd2a4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461497} {:answer/id #uuid "508f9c1d-ff37-59ea-8879-8c3b43a99d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "508f9c1d-ff37-59ea-8879-8c3b43a99d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461498} :answer-field/id #uuid "d05f7a7f-f105-54d3-b92a-8e85aaa18df5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462502} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10df3356-aa72-55c4-bcd3-8b55d0e35022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461499} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3cf18f-98e0-5531-8398-e40d7d3f3583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae3cf18f-98e0-5531-8398-e40d7d3f3583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461500} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a30126-3bf0-5ebf-853d-b9c28b6450dc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462503} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70c6c33b-acc0-53d0-83fb-1320d1026d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461501} {:answer/id #uuid "55465f4e-feef-55e7-aee1-cf9db4d48e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70c6c33b-acc0-53d0-83fb-1320d1026d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461501} :answer-field/id #uuid "a96caab2-f5ca-53aa-b65f-98a419247edb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f464429f-4905-5c37-b6cf-d2ce0cb09dd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-108911" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n- **I.** ${y}^{′}-\\sqrt{x}\\,y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}$\n- **II.** ${y}^{′}+y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}$ $$\n- **III.** ${y}^{′}-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x={y}^{6}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\sqrt{x},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=-1.\n$$\n\n- Equation II is a Bernoulli differential equation. In this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,\\,q(x)=-\\sqrt{x},\\,n=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only."} {:db/id 17592186244192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eef27d2b-6149-5070-b711-f4dcc7db2a03" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}] :question/answer