nt/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a64257-013e-5f8d-b152-d9e7634b93e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461521} {:answer/id #uuid "44f88025-dd1b-5198-a95d-7ba9a5e96e82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25a64257-013e-5f8d-b152-d9e7634b93e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461521} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4513080-f5de-5d9a-b8bd-7e3281ab4ff6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462514} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "002f52a6-9b40-5817-806e-04c903f93628" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461523} {:answer/id #uuid "f65c2b84-64a9-52f6-9a3b-93f218800c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f65c2b84-64a9-52f6-9a3b-93f218800c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461524} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4d9626a-f524-53e7-923d-73b8234b228b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462515} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e652a4bd-a6e3-5008-b2e6-7bbfef7cb7ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461525} {:answer/id #uuid "eda70d64-65fd-54ee-82af-095577f34912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e652a4bd-a6e3-5008-b2e6-7bbfef7cb7ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461525} :answer-field/id #uuid "83fc44fd-f73d-55e3-a891-ad000c8c31b2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d4b7e54f-2216-5cba-ba81-1d5ec0ebc609" :question/math-academy-id "q-108918" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n- **I.** ${y}^{′}-{e}^{x}{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{y}$\n- **II.** ${y}^{3}{y}^{′}+{y}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=\\sqrt{y}$\n- **III.** $y\\,{y}^{′}+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={cos}^{2}⁡y$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is a real number.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. It is missing the $p(x)y$ term.\n\n- Equation II is a Bernoulli differential equation. Writing the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y={y}^{-5/2}\n$$\n\nwhich is a Bernoulli differential equation with\n\n$$\np(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\\,q(x)=1,\\,n=-\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation.  If we attempt to write the equation in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+x(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}{y})=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡y}{y}.\n$$\n\nIt is missing both the $p(x)y$ and $q(x){y}^{n}$ terms.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}
